\begin_layout Standard
Before noon:
 Investigators’ surveillance review indicated that a vehicle registered to the defendant arrived on campus.
 The defendant allegedly visited campus multiple times that day,
 including two visits before the shooting.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Shortly before noon:
 The defendant allegedly returned to campus wearing different clothing but the same shoes and walking with a limp.
 Surveillance footage reportedly showed him walking toward the stairs leading to the Losee Building roof.
 Investigators concluded that he was the person captured on that footage;
 his roommate,
 Lance Twiggs,
 reportedly said still images “definitely” looked like the defendant.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
After the event began,
 before 12:23 p.m.:
 Kirk seated himself beneath a canopy tent on the west side of the amphitheater,
 below the Hall of Flags.
 An attendee stood directly in front of him to ask a question.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Approximately 12:23:28 p.m.:
 While the attendee was questioning Kirk,
 a shot was fired.
 The bullet struck the left side of Kirk’s neck and killed him.
 The document describes the bullet’s path as front-to-back,
 slightly left-to-right,
 and downward.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
At the moment of the shot:
 UVU Officer Christopher Bagley—
not “Bailey,” as the earlier summary stated—
was positioned on the south end of the Hall of Flags walkway roof,
 above Kirk’s canopy.
 Based on his firearms experience,
 Bagley believed the shot came from a rifle fired east of the canopy.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Immediately afterward:
 Surveillance footage allegedly showed a man on the Losee Building roof stand up,
 run northeast across the roof carrying a long,
 narrow black object,
 and descend from the northeast side.
 He then crossed Campus Drive and entered a wooded area north of the road.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Shortly afterward:
 Police recovered a Mauser Model 98 rifle chambered in .30-06 Springfield,
 with a telescopic sight,
 wrapped in a black towel in the wooded area.
 The excerpt says the rifle was operable.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Roof evidence:
 Bagley found a screwdriver near the roof’s guardrail and disturbances in the gravel at the southwest edge consistent with a “sniper pad”—
a prone position with a line of sight to Kirk’s seat.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Later investigation:
 DNA testing reportedly provided strong or supportive evidence that the defendant contributed DNA found on the screwdriver,
 towel,
 rifle,
 and fired cartridge casing.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Approximately 12:36 a.m.,
 September 11,
 2025:
 The defendant allegedly returned to the intersection of Campus Drive and 800 South,
